# x86/ARM machine with ~64 GB RAM and no usable GPU (pure CPU, or an iGPU left unused).
# Only MoE models with few active params: dense 27B on CPU decodes at a few tok/s.
# Budget (MemTotal ~62 GiB), both chat models resident at once:
#   coder     Qwen3.6-35B-A3B heretic i1-Q6_K 26.5 GiB resident (0.65 GiB MTP layer skipped at load)
#             + KV 128K 2.5 + DeltaNet checkpoints <=1.0 + ~1.5 compute + 3 prompt cache = ~34.5 GiB
#   architect gpt-oss-20b heretic-ara-v3 MXFP4 11.3 GiB + KV 64K 1.5 + SWA checkpoints ~0.15 + ~1.5 compute
#             + 3 cache (cap; its full 64K state is ~1.5) = ~17.4 GiB
#   embed + rerank at 8K ~3.5 GiB          total ~55.5 GiB, ~6.5 GiB left for the OS and OpenCode
# The 3 GiB prompt-cache cap holds one full 128K coder state (~2.6 GiB), so a reviewer subagent on the coder
# does not force a multi-minute re-prefill of the main conversation.
# Q8_0 instead of Q6_K would leave under 1 GiB: it does not fit beside the architect.
# The architect is a second model from a different lineage for plans and reviews, in the same speed class
# (3.6B active). Its reasoning effort stays at the template default (medium); "high" on CPU means
# multi-minute answers. gpt-oss caveats: "architect:fast" only lowers reasoning_effort to low (harmony has
# no thinking-off switch), and its template silently drops a system message that is not the first one.
# Stock aliases go to a separate exclusive group: loading one unloads the uncensored pair first.
# Not benchmarked on CPU yet. A cold re-prefill near 128K takes many minutes; lower the coder ctx if that hurts.
PROFILE_DESC="CPU only, ~64 GB RAM"

# alias=catalog_id@ctx[@extra llama-server args]
# Aliases are stable API model names; harness configs only ever reference aliases.
ULA_MODELS="
coder=qwen3.6-35b-a3b-heretic-q6k@131072
architect=gpt-oss-20b-heretic-ara-mxfp4@65536
coder-stock=qwen3.6-35b-a3b-q6k@131072
architect-stock=gpt-oss-20b-mxfp4@65536
embed=qwen3-embedding-0.6b-q8@8192
rerank=qwen3-reranker-0.6b-q8@8192
"
# Installed by default; the rest with `ula pull --all` or `install.sh --all-models`.
ULA_DEFAULT="coder architect embed rerank"

ULA_CODER=coder
ULA_ARCHITECT=architect
ULA_SWAP_LLMS=false         # coder and architect fit side by side
ULA_GPU_ARGS=""             # CPU. A Vulkan/ROCm build still offloads to an iGPU by default (-ngl auto); ULA_ACCEL=cpu avoids that
ULA_CHAT_ARGS="--cache-ram 3072"   # per server process (a cap, not a reservation); two run at once
ULA_TTL=1800                # unload an idle chat model after 30 min
ULA_MIN_DISK_GIB=10
